    "note": [
      "[b]Outdoor recreation[/b]\r\n\r\n[b]How do we measure this?[/b]\r\nPercentage of households with accessible natural space within 400 metres. The indicator includes accessible natural space spanning two hectares or more, as well as off-road trails throughout Northern Ireland. It encompasses natural spaces accessible to the public with permission from the landowners, including urban and rural parks, forests, beaches, and off-road trails.\r\n\r\n[b]Source[/b]\r\nNorthern Ireland Environment Statistics Report, Department of Agriculture, Environment and Rural Affairs\r\n[url=https://www.daera-ni.gov.uk/articles/northern-ireland-environmental-statistics-report]https://www.daera-ni.gov.uk/articles/northern-ireland-environmental-statistics-report[/url]\r\n\r\n[b]Impact of Covid-19[/b]\r\nDuring the Covid-19 pandemic people relied on outdoor physical activities for their daily exercise. This highlighted the need for safe, high quality, accessible and welcoming natural spaces and places.\r\n\r\n[b]Further information[/b]\r\n1. Includes accessible natural space over two hectares and off-road routes, such as urban and country parks, forests, beaches and walking trails."
